e","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"Write \\(p=u_x\\), \\(q=u_y\\), and \\(F=pq-u\\). Charpit’s equations are\n\\[\n\\dot x=F_p=q,\\qquad \\dot y=F_q=p,\\qquad\n\\dot u=pF_p+qF_q=2pq,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\dot p=-F_x-pF_u=p,\\qquad\n\\dot q=-F_y-qF_u=q.\n\\]\n\nAt \\(s=0\\), the initial curve gives\n\\[\nq(0,\\tau)=\\frac{d}{d\\tau}(\\tau^2)=2\\tau,\n\\qquad p(0,\\tau)q(0,\\tau)=\\tau^2.\n\\]\nThus \\(p(0,\\tau)=\\tau/2\\) for \\(\\tau\\ne0\\), with the same value at \\(\\tau=0\\) by continuous extension. Hence\n\\[\np=\\frac{\\tau}{2}e^s,\\qquad q=2\\tau e^s.\n\\]\nIntegrating with \\(x(0)=0,\\ y(0)=\\tau,\\ u(0)=\\tau^2\\) yields\n\\[\nx=2\\tau(e^s-1),\\qquad\ny=\\frac{\\tau}{2}(e^s+1),\\qquad\nu=\\tau^2e^{2s}.\n\\]\nAt \\(\\tau=0\\), this family gives the stationary characteristic; the initial constraints at that single point alone are degenerate.\n\nFinal answer: **Option 3**, \\(x=2\\tau(e^s-1),\\ y=\\dfrac{\\tau}{2}(e^s+1),\\ u=\\tau^2e^{2s}\\)."}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h","reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","store":false,"temperature":1,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":0}},"tools":[],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":0.98,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":371,"input_tokens_details":{"cache_write_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":0},"output_tokens":564,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":184},"total_tokens":935},"user":null,"metadata":{}}
